I tested it and it worked in Chrome, but in Firefox I had to force the use of OGG because it simply didn't produce any sound:
JavaScript:
AudioManager.audioFileExt = function() {
    return '.ogg';
};
Only do this if you have full knowledge of how to back up or restore the original files. In my case, I only did it with the content that comes with RPG Maker, not the add-ons:
Spoiler
Another thing I did was reduce the quality of all the OGG files after deleting the M4A files using FFMPEG. So, it went from 163 MB to 27 MB. Since none of the songs have vocals, the quality isn't bad; I tested it on different devices
